.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A modern, policy‑driven dynamic Vector container that provides fast indexed access, optional auto‑growth, insertion, removal, traversal, and multiple zero‑overhead reinterpretation views\&. 

These views allow the same underlying Vector to be interpreted as a span, a sorted set, a multiset, an unordered set, or a search helper — without copying or allocating additional memory\&.

.PP
Beginners: 
.br
 Think of \fBVector<T>\fP as a dynamic array that can instantly transform into different “shapes” such as a set, a multiset, or a span, depending on what you need\&. 

.PP
Professionals: 
.br
 \fBVector<T>\fP follows a modern C++‑style multi‑view design\&. Ordering is defined by \fBISimpleCompare<T>\fP strategies, sorting is controlled by SortAction<TCompare, TContainer> policies, and all reinterpretations are zero‑overhead wrappers\&. 
.br
 This enables policy‑based sorting, strategy‑based comparison, and flexible container semantics without hidden allocations or implicit behavior\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The element type stored in the Vector\&.
.RE
.PP

